- op: discuss  # 9b8f
  at: '2026-08-05T10:20:18Z'  # 9b8f
  by: agent  # 9b8f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9b8f
  clock: 3  # 9b8f
  nonce: 9b8f  # 9b8f
  message: "IMPLEMENTED AND MERGED 2026-08-05, PR #216 (dev 5993042f18). Each dead-code-maybe candidate\nnow carries a reachability cohort: test_only, unreachable, or null under a non-default seed\nmode where no test-seeded walk ran. Null rather than a default, because \"the walk did not\nrun\" and \"it ran and found nobody\" are different facts, and defaulting would assert one the\ntool never computed -- which is the shape of the defect this field exists to fix. Text mode\nannotates the line, since a disclosure that exists only under --json is half shipped.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, self-tree, through the real CLI on the merged code:\n    hypergumbo dead-code-maybe . --input <selfmap> --format json\n    schema_version 0.2.0, view dead_code_maybe\n    test_only_reachable             1859   (over all production symbols)\n    test_only_reachable_candidates  1747   (over emitted candidates)\n    summed per-item labels          1747   EXACT MATCH\nThe item's filed figures were 1851 of 2094; they now read 1859 / 1747 / 2107.\n\nTHE FILING PROPOSED THREE VALUES AND ONE OF THEM IS MEANINGLESS. It suggested test_only /\nentrypoint_only / unreachable. A dead candidate is BY DEFINITION unreachable from the\nproduction seeds, and those are a superset of the entrypoint seeds, so every dead candidate\nis entrypoint-only-dead by construction and that label would partition nothing.\nentrypoint_only_dead stays a summary count of a different, larger cohort: 4314 against 2107.\nThe per-candidate discriminator is binary. Another instance of the filed remedy being a\nhypothesis, this time in its vocabulary rather than its mechanism.\n\nA SECOND DENOMINATOR SHIPPED WITH IT, BECAUSE MY FIRST TEST ASSERTED A FALSE EQUALITY AND\nPASSED. It compared the summed per-item labels against test_only_reachable. Those are two\ndifferent populations: the summary counts over ALL production symbols, while the emitted\ncandidate list has the FP demoters applied (generated files, cross-language name hits,\nvirtual-dispatch overrides, the --exclude-* filters). The fixture is small enough that no\ndemoter fires, so the two happened to be equal and the assertion held. On the self-tree they\nare 1859 against 1747 -- a 112-symbol gap that would have shipped as a false equality nobody\ncould reproduce from the fixture. Caught by measuring on a real repository, not by the test.\nBoth numbers are now published and the test asserts the relationship that is actually\ninvariant: the candidate-scoped count is exact and can only be <= the production-scoped one.\nThat is L60 -- count the shape and count the consumer separately; they are different\ndenominators and only one is usually measured.\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN CLOSING INSTRUCTION IS HONOURED: no --seeds all flag, no documentation-only\nchange. The information WAS still available at emission time -- the set was being computed\nand collapsed to a len() on the way out, which is the first of the two possibilities the\nfiling asked us to distinguish.\n\nWHY IT LANDED NOW: it is WI-ratuv's prerequisite. A gate needs per-item attribution to key\non, and every number in WI-ratuv's re-scoping note was measured through this field. None of\nit was answerable before."  # 9b8f
